# fh101, the riddler by the wall (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle fh101
revision 1
state ready
dialect frosthollow
accent none
tier standard
written_for cty_marl_craghearth
written_by claude
title the riddler by the wall
fits stage=adult|old
prefers talk=quiet warmth=warm
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=warm humour=none honesty=guarded piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk never_sits_with_a_back_to_the_door
likes plum_tart riddles festival_bells warm_rain
dislikes gulls bad_manners
fears a_clamp_breaking_out_in_the_night a_door_opening_behind_me
hopes a_quiet_hearth_with_the_door_in_sight a_riddle_nobody_can_answer
topics pastimes +0.4 work +0.3 festival +0.3 food +0.2 home +0.2 gossip -0.5
styles comfort=quiet gossip=closed refuse=soft tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# burns charcoal up at the hearths and always takes the seat facing the door: quiet, warm and close-mouthed, slow to say a thing twice, with a riddle kept back for anyone who sits long enough.

words
oath! = Back to the wall | Eyes on the latch | Door and corner
saying! = A shut mouth gathers no dust | Sit where the door can't surprise you | Answer late and answer once
door = the door | that door
seat = my corner | the seat by the wall
latch = the latch | the door latch
riddle = a riddle | a good riddle
tart = plum tart | a slice of plum tart
tin = the tart tin | the tin on the high shelf
clamp = the clamp | the burning stack
skin = the turf skin | the sods over the clamp
charcoal = charcoal | good black charcoal
hearths = the hearths | the upper hearths
bells = the feast bells | bells on a feast day
softrain = warm rain | a soft warm rain
gulls = gulls | those gulls
mm = Mm | Hm
well = the old well | the well at the top of the lane
smoke = the smoke | the clamp smoke

any
opinion @1 city against 1 : Too many doors in a city, and every one at your back. #mm#. I'll stay up here.
opinion @1 merchants against 2 : The bread goes up a penny and nobody can tell me why. Not a word of it is in my pocket.
opinion @1 houses against 1 : The Houses want a back to bend, not a face to know. I keep mine straight and stay out of their way.
opinion @1 dole for 1 : A town this small can spare a bowl. Nobody should lie down #hungry# in the #cold#.
opinion @1 times against 1 : Each week the pot's a bit lighter, and the ones up the hill never look down. #saying#.
opinion @1 strangers mixed 1 : I'll nod to a stranger. I'll not turn my back on one till I've seen them eat.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. Sit if you like. Not that chair. | #greet#, #address#. Come in where I can see you.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes self.job=none] : #greet#. Stand upwind of #clamp#. | #greet#. Talk if you want. I'm watching the smoke.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. The frost's still on #latch#. | Morning, #address#. Early for both of us.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#. Shut #door# behind you. | #greet#. Late to be out, #address#.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : There you are. I kept you the stool by the fire, #address#. | You. Sit. There's #tart# left, just.
line @1 again.open : You again. #good.capitalize#. The chair's still free. | Twice in a day. I'll start keeping you a seat.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#, #address#.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family|housemates] : #greet#. Pull a stool round this side. | #greet#. I saw you at #door# before you knocked.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : #greet#. Mind the smoke. | #greet#. I'll talk, but I'm watching #clamp#.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#. Bring the lamp in with you. | #greet#. Late one.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. | #farewell#. Mind the step down.
line @2 farewell [here.time=dusk|night] : #farewell#. Keep to the middle of the lane. | #farewell#. Bar #door# when you're home.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | #farewell#, #address#.
line @1 react.news.new : #surprise#. I'd not heard a word. | #mm#. That's new to me.
line @1 react.news.known : I'd heard. Not from who you'd think. | #knew#. I kept it to myself.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I'll wait to hear that twice before I believe it once. | #doubt#. I've heard louder things come to nothing.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : #pity#. I'm sorry for them. | That's #very# hard. I'll say nothing light about it.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : #gladnews#. I'll take #tart# round. | #good.capitalize#. Somebody's luck turned, then.
line @1 answer.how : Well enough. #tired.capitalize#, but well. | #fine#. Can't grumble, so I won't.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : #busy.capitalize#. #clamp.capitalize#'s burning wrong and I'm the one awake. | Watching #smoke#. It's harder than it sounds.
line @1 ask.how : And yourself? Eating? | How are you keeping, #address#?
line @1 sympathise : #sympathy#. Sit with me a while. You needn't talk. | Here. Have the warm side. #sympathy#.
line @1 reassure : #reassure#. Things settle, given time. | It'll pass, #address#. Most things do, if you let them.
line @1 decline : #hedge#. I'd come, but #clamp# won't watch itself tonight. | Not this time, #address#. I'm promised elsewhere, and a promise holds.
line @1 accept_decline : #no_matter#. Another day. | That's all right. The offer keeps.
line @1 thank : #thanks#. I'll remember it. | That was #good# of you, #address#.
line @1 deflect_thanks : #deflect#. You'd have done the same. | Nothing to it.
line @1 preclose [self.working=yes] : Well. #clamp.capitalize# wants looking at. | I'd best see to #skin# before it cracks.
line @2 preclose : Well. #preclose#. | I'll be off home before the light goes.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go on, then. | #bc_right#
line @1 ack : #mm#. | #bc_right#
line @1 give.advice : Sit where you can see the room. You'd be surprised what you learn. | Say it once, plainly, and then stop. #saying#.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : #warn#. Don't walk the pass alone this week. | Keep off the road after dark, #address#.
rule @door_bark
when concept=bark working=no
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Who left #door# wide? #oath#. | Somebody's at #latch#. #mm#. Only the wind.

rule @clamp_bark
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=none here.region=frosthollow
does aside
cooldown 6h
say #clamp.capitalize#'s breathing too fast. More turf on the windward side. | Smoke's gone blue. #oath#. Somebody fetch a shovel.

rule @rain_bark
when concept=bark here.weather=rain here.season=spring|summer
does aside
cooldown 10h
say #softrain.capitalize#. I'll stand in it a minute. | Rain like a warm bath. That's my weather.

rule @bells_bark
when concept=bark here.day=festival
does aside
cooldown 12h
say There go #bells#. #good.capitalize#. | #bells.capitalize#. I'd get up for those, any morning.

scene door_seat
when topic=smalltalk|home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : That's my seat, facing #door#. Take any other. | I'll swap with you, if you'll sit there. I like to see #latch#. | Everyone asks why I sit like this, facing #door#.
b : What's wrong with this one? | Why the latch? | Well, why do you?
a : Nothing. It just has its back to #door#. | I like to know who's at #latch# before they know I'm here. | Because a door opens, sooner or later. I'd like to see it when it does.
b : #bc_fair_enough# | Fair enough. | #bc_wise#

scene riddle_lamp
when topic=pastimes
does raise / ask.detail / answer.detail / laugh
a : Here's #riddle#. I eat and eat, and the more I eat the hungrier I grow. Give me a drink and I die. | Try this. I've a mouth and never speak, a bed and never sleep. | One for you. The more of me you take, the more of me you leave behind.
b : A pig? No. Is it fire? | Is it a river? | Is it money?
a : Fire. You're quicker than you look, #address#. | A river. Most folk say a drunkard first. #mm#. | No. Footsteps. Mind you don't take too many in #snow#.
b : #bc_ha# | Ha. I'd have said a drunkard. | #bc_clever#

scene riddle_back
when topic=pastimes pair.band=friends|family|housemates
does tell.self / challenge / concede / insist / ack
a : I've had #riddle# going round my head since #supper#. Nobody's got it yet. | You never got last week's. I'll not tell you the answer. | I made a new one up at #clamp# last night. It's a hard one.
b : Try me. I'll get it. | I worked it out. It was a shadow. | Then ask me. I'm sharp tonight.
a : What has one eye and sees nothing? A needle. You'd not have got it. | #oath#. A shadow it was. Who told you? | What gets wetter the more it dries? Take your time.
b : I'd have got it. | Nobody. I'm cleverer than you think. | A towel. Easy.
a : You'd not. #bc_ha# | Then I'll make #riddle# harder still. | #mm#. I'll do better tomorrow.

scene clamp_night
when topic=work self.working=yes self.job=none here.region=frosthollow
does tell.self / react.self / assess / ack
a : Three nights I've sat by #clamp#. You learn its breathing like a sick friend's. | I sleep in the hut by #hearths# when a burn's on. Sleep's the wrong word. | You watch #smoke# all night. White is good. Blue means trouble.
b : Three nights? | Do you sleep at all? | And when it goes blue?
a : Three. Wood goes in, #charcoal# comes out, and in between you sit. | In pieces. An ear open, always. | Then you run with turf and a shovel for #skin#, and you don't stop.
b? : #bc_poor_soul# | #bc_i_know# | #bc_wise#

scene clamp_breaking
when topic=work self.working=yes self.job=none here.region=frosthollow here.weather=storm|clear
does tell.worry / reassure / assess / ack
a : The wind got under #skin# last night. Flame came through on the north side. | I patched #clamp# twice before dawn. If it breaks out, a week's wood is ash. | A clamp that catches proper burns to nothing. I'll not let it.
b : You caught it in time. | #reassure# | You won't.
a : This time. I'll sit closer tonight. | It held. My paws don't think so. | No. Not while I'm awake.
b? : #bc_good# | #bc_lucky# | #bc_hope_so#

scene black_paws
when topic=health|work self.job=none self.working=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Look at these paws. Black to the elbow with #charcoal#. It won't come out till spring. | My eyes sting from #smoke# all day. They stop at night, mostly. | I cough up #charcoal# some mornings. Everyone at #hearths# does.
b : Scrub them. | Does it hurt? | That can't be good.
a : I did. It's not dirt any more. It's me. | Not much. #mm#. I'm used to it. | No. But it's the work, and the work feeds us.

scene tart_tin
when topic=food
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : There's #tart# in #tin#. I keep it up high where hands can't wander. | #tart.capitalize#'s the one thing I'll queue for. | I had the last of #tart# for breakfast. I'm not sorry.
b : Can I have some? | Why plum? | For breakfast?
a : A slice. Don't tell the rest of the house about #tin#. | Plums are sour till they're cooked. Then they're the best thing there is. | Breakfast, #supper#, any hour. It's never the wrong time.
b : #bc_thank_you# | #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_ha#

scene tart_shared
when topic=food|friends pair.band=friends|family|housemates
does offer / accept / assess
a : Here. I saved you a corner of #tart#. | I've #tin# under my arm. Don't ask where I'm going with it. | Sit. There's #tart#, and I won't eat it all if you're watching.
b : You saved me some? | Where are you going with it? | Then I'll watch.
a : I did. I don't, often. Eat it before I change my mind. | To you, as it happens. Here. | #good.capitalize#. Have the bigger slice, then.

scene warm_rain
when topic=weather here.weather=rain here.season=spring|summer
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #softrain.capitalize#. I'd stand out in it all day if they let me. | Smell that? The dust going down under #softrain#. | After a dry week, rain like this is a kindness.
b : You'll be soaked. | I can smell it. | I'd sooner be dry.
a : It's warm. Soaked doesn't count when it's warm. | #good.capitalize#. Then we've both smelled it. | You're welcome to dry. I'll stay out here.

scene cold_sleet
when topic=weather here.weather=rain here.season=autumn|winter
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : That's not rain, that's ice that can't decide. | #rain.capitalize# again. It finds the gap at the back of my collar. | The good rain's a summer thing. This is the other kind.
b : #cold.capitalize#, too. | Every collar. | It is.
a : Bone-deep. I'll be in #seat# by the fire. | Every one. #mm#. | Give me the warm kind, or nothing.

scene snow_door
when topic=weather|home here.weather=snow
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Snow up to #latch# this morning. I dug #door# out before I could see it. | #snow.capitalize#. Everything's quiet. You hear anyone coming a long way off. | I like #snow#. Footprints tell you who's been by.
b : Before breakfast? | Quiet's nice. | Who's been by, then?
a : Before anything. A door you can't open is no door, #address#. | Quiet's safe. That's why it's nice. | Nobody I didn't expect. #good.capitalize#.

scene dawn_frost
when topic=day|weather here.time=dawn here.season=winter|autumn
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Frost on everything. Even the inside of the window. | Up before the light again. #clamp.capitalize# doesn't care what hour it is. | I like the dark before dawn. Nobody's about to surprise you.
b : Inside? | Nor does anything else. | That's one way to look at it.
a : Inside. I scratched my name off it. Then I put it back. | No. You get used to it, or you don't stay. | It's my way, #address#.

scene feast_bells
when topic=festival|season self.likes=festival_bells
does tell.feeling / ask.opinion / give.opinion / assess
a : I wake for #bells# even when I've sat up all night. | When #bells# go I stand at #door# and listen till the last one stops. | Nothing in the year sounds like #bells#.
b : All night, and you still get up? | Every time? | You like the bells that much?
a : Every year. Sleep can wait. #bells.capitalize# won't. | Every time. I don't know why. I've stopped asking. | More than the food, and I like the food.
b? : #bc_lovely# | #bc_every_year# | #bc_fair_enough#

scene bad_manners
when topic=smalltalk|friends
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Somebody walked in yesterday without knocking and sat in #seat#. Didn't even say good day. | A wolf spat in the lane in front of me. I said nothing. I'm still saying nothing. | Manners cost nothing. That's why I notice when they're missing.
b : And what did you do? | Rude of them. | They do cost nothing.
a : Stood behind them till they moved. It didn't take long. | Rude, and they'll be rude again. I'll know them. | Nothing at all. And still some folk won't pay it.

scene the_well
when topic=home|gossip here.region=frosthollow
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : See #well#? Half the street says it's theirs. | Folk have quarrelled over #well# since before I was born. | I won't say who's right about #well#. I'll only say I draw from it.
b : Whose is it, then? | What's the quarrel? | And do they let you?
a : Nobody's. That's the trouble. Everybody wants to be the one who owns nobody's well. | Who dug it, who mended it, who drinks first. All of it and none of it. | I don't ask. #saying#.
b? : #bc_ha# | #bc_poor_soul# | #bc_wise#

scene spouse_quiet
when topic=family self.married=yes
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #self.spouse# is the one soul I'll sit with my back to a door for. | I don't say much. I think #self.spouse# likes me the better for it. | I'd not trade #self.spouse# for all the tart on the hill.
b : That's love, then. | Lucky. | All of it?
a : #mm#. I'd not say it so loud. | #very.capitalize# lucky. I know it. | Most of it. Don't repeat that.

scene full_house
when topic=home pair.band=housemates
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A full house, and I'm the only one who checks #latch# twice at night. | Every chair in our house is spoken for. Mine faces #door#. Nobody argues now. | It's loud with all of us in. I like it more than I let on, #address#.
b : Somebody has to. | Nobody dares. | You do hide it.
a : Somebody does. It's me. | They learned. #good.capitalize#. | I hide most things. That's the trick of it.

scene gossip_kept
when topic=gossip|crime
does tell.gossip / react.news / insist / ack
a : I heard something by #hearths#. I'll not say what. | You'd be surprised what I hear from #seat#. I keep it there. | Somebody told me a thing yesterday. It was theirs to tell, not mine.
b : Go on. Just the start. | Like what? | Fair enough.
a : No. Not the start, not the end. It'll keep. | Things folk say when they think nobody's listening. That's all you'll get. | It's the only way anyone ever tells me anything.
b : #bc_ha# | Ha. #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_wise#

scene stranger_watch
when topic=newcomer|player
does tell.self / react.self / assess / ack
a : There's a new face about. I watched them come up the lane. | A stranger came in and stood with their back to #door#. Brave, or new. | I don't mind strangers. I like to see them first, is all.
b : What did you make of them? | Which was it? | You see everyone first.
a : Too early to say. I'll watch a while longer. | New. Nobody here would do it twice. | That's the idea, #address#.
b? : #bc_maybe# | #bc_ha# | #bc_wise#

scene faith_bells
when topic=faith
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : I say a word to the Bright One at #door# every morning. Short. It doesn't need long. | I'm no chapel-goer, but I go when #bells# ring. | I keep my prayers like my business. Quiet, and to one listener.
b : What do you say? | Only for the bells? | That's prayer enough.
a : Keep the roof up and #clamp# lit. That's the whole of it. | The bells, and the warm. #mm#. And the singing, a bit. | I hope so. It's the only kind I've got.

scene hard_times
when topic=times|prices world.times=hard|lean
does tell.worry / react.complaint / reassure / ack
a : Bread's up again. I've stopped asking why. #mm#. | Less in the pot this week. Nobody at home says it, but we all see it. | The wood costs more and #charcoal# fetches the same. I don't do the sums any more.
b : Everyone's short. | #bc_i_know# | You'd rather not know.
a : #bc_i_know#. Doesn't fill the pot. | We'll manage. We always have. #reassure#. | No. I'd rather sleep.
b? : #bc_true# | #bc_hope_so# | #bc_fair_enough#

story grandad_riddle [topic=memories|pastimes self.age>=25]
  : My #grandad# never gave a straight answer in his life. Ask him the time and he'd give you a riddle.
  : He told me one when I was small and never told me the answer. He died with it.
  ask : Shall I tell you it? You might be the one who gets it.
  b : Go on, then. I'll try.
  b[old] : I knew a wolf like that once. Go on.
  : What's always coming and never arrives? I've had forty answers. None of them sounded like his.

story gull_tart [topic=memories|animals self.age>=25]
  : I went down to the lake once, years back. Sat on the shore with a slice of #tart#.
  : A gull came out of nowhere and took it clean out of my paw. Didn't even slow down.
  ask : Do you know what I did?
  b : You chased it, I'd bet.
  b[stage=young] : Did you throw a stone at it?
  : I sat there, sore and hungry, and I swore I'd never trust a bird again. I haven't. #gulls.capitalize# know what they did.

story first_burn [topic=work|memories self.job=none self.age>=25]
  : My first burn, I turned my back on #clamp# to eat. One minute, no more.
  : When I turned round, flame was coming out of #skin# like a door left open.
  ask : Can you guess what I learned that night?
  b : Not to turn your back.
  b[job=miner] : To eat standing up, I'd say.
  : Never to turn my back on anything. Not #clamp#, not #door#. I've not since.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. Come round this side, where I can see you. | #greet#, #address#. What is it?
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. You know which chair's mine. Take another. | #topic.player#. #good.capitalize#. Sit down.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : It's late. Shut #door# and say it quick.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : Say what you want from there by #door#. I can hear you fine.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=none self.working=yes] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. You sit up with the burn, and you don't take your eyes off the smoke. | I make #charcoal#. Slow work, and #cold# at night.
dlg @2 resident.job : I work, I come home, I sit facing #door#. That's most of me.
dlg @1 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : #news_none# And if there were, you'd not get it from me first.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : #gossip_none# | I hear things from #seat#. I keep them.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Mind #door# on your way out. | #farewell#, #address#.
graft resident.hub
choice Why do you always sit facing the door? -> door
node door
say Habit. Old habit. A door opens, sooner or later, and I'd sooner see it. #mm#. That's all I'll say about it.
mood calm
free
choice Have you a riddle for me instead? -> riddle
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node riddle
say All right. What can you hold in your left paw but never in your right? Think about it. Come back with the answer.
mood pleased
choice I'll think on it. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
